{:db/id 17592186175910 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186175736 :question/id #uuid "4dd86f6d-270f-5942-b7cf-df53a0bf4ee4" :question/math-academy-id "e-14361" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0,1)$ and is parallel to the line $y=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5$." :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{2}{3}x + 5\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nthat passes through the point $(0,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{2}{3}(x - 0) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{2}{3}x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3}x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4dcbc520-40b5-5c08-ba56-be105c135240" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049716 :topic/math-academy-id 1240 :topic/title "Equations of Lines in Slope-Intercept Form"} {:db/id 17592186050245 :topic/math-academy-id 837 :topic/title "Parallel Lines in the Coordinate Plane"} {:db/id 17592186050635 :topic/math-academy-id 418 :topic/title "Equations of Lines in Point-Slope Form"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186176423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "20f45c71-4449-5cf6-9933-4eba8f82dccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186174747}] :question/id #uuid "10c44579-dc85-566b-8520-b63fbd992d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-215701" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4d7c284501bcfffef9626c71e3d768e3edd6b295f4228ee576f647e8cf6d4e9.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y = \\frac{1}{2}x$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?$y =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id 17592186176490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "857666d7-78f8-5db5-a976-bfbb90b20f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-x - 1" :db/id 17592186175079} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2be2ce-4b87-5f0d-a17c-01c13c08c89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = x + 1" :db/id 17592186175080} {:answer/id #uuid "b25787de-333a-5901-aa2d-38ee9e940162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-x + 1" :db/id 17592186175081} {:answer/id #uuid "b95b4071-0e5d-5e96-9a5e-f40faa0d6f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = x" :db/id 17592186175082} {:answer/id #uuid "352267a4-bc55-522d-81b9-edb8d934abe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-x" :db/id 17592186175083}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cf2361b1-7b2e-57ca-9750-c20bd3fcd619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186175078}] :question/id #uuid "ca38fd84-40dd-56ec-b024-482435371d75" :question/math-academy-id "q-44399" :question/problem "![](images/86/86d6eae2f6bec9ef31d993d09aa56cbca88432678e10e3fa8b4ef72b4058077b.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y =-x + 3$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Passing Through a Point"}
